-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SURFACE IMPLEMENTATION (parity port; no stubs / no placeholder / no skeleton-only)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Native WinUI 3 port of the web ReleaseNotes export: a compact, single-expansion release-notes
  accordion. Newest `limit` releases (web default 3) rendered as disclosure cards; each header carries a
  badge-tinted Segoe Fluent "Gift" glyph (\uE8C9, native stand-in for the web Lucide Gift), the v{version}
  label, a TsBadge (latest/stable/beta), and the release date; each expanded body repeats the localized
  "What's New" heading over the release's FLAT, author-ordered change list (NOT grouped into sections,
  matching the web), every line prefixed by a ChangelogChangeType-coloured dot.
- DRY / single source of truth: binds the shared P1/S8 IChangelogSource and reuses the embedded
  ChangelogCatalog + ChangelogEntry/Change/Badge/ChangeType from TeslaSync.App.ModalsDialogs -- the native
  analogue of the web @/generated/changelog module both ReleaseNotes and ChangelogModal read. No catalog
  duplication (the web component's stated purpose: "no drift between three hand-curated lists").
- ALL states render (no hidden surfaces): loading (skeleton), loaded (accordion list), empty (TsEmptyState
  with Gift glyph), error (TsQueryError + retry), stale (Warning chip), offline (Neutral chip + cached list)
  -- routed through the shared cache-then-network RepositoryResult<ChangelogReading> seam, exactly like the
  sibling ChangelogModal models the same static catalog.
- Single-expansion accordion (web `expanded` single-value useState): ExpandedVersion in the view-model,
  newest release open by default, opening one card collapses the others (TsAccordion/Expander coordination),
  a user's choice survives refreshes (web useState initialiser semantics).
- i18n: every string resolves through the P1/S10 ILocalizer facade with `translation.`-prefixed keys, ALL
  present in Strings/en/Resources.resw:
    translation.changelog.releaseNotes.heading ("What's New")
    translation.changelog.badges.{latest,stable,beta}
    translation.common.{noData,retry,stale,offline,loading}  translation.error.serverError.message
  No hardcoded English literal in native code (English appears only as ILocalizer fallbacks).
- Accessibility: TsAccordion exposes the ExpandCollapse pattern; every entry header carries a Narrator name
  ("v0.7.0, Latest, 2026-03-29"); the badge is named; the Gift glyph is AccessibilityView.Raw (decorative);
  loading/empty/error are live regions; reduce-motion is honoured (skeleton pulse suppressed); custom
  Group automation peer with a heading name fallback.
- Telemetry: ReleaseNotesDiagnostics emits view.opened slug=ReleaseNotes once on load (P1/S11), PII-safe.

